    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312-a1">

                <pb facs="0544" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg526"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Senator Tom Connolly
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-10">February 10,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Senator Connally</hi>: As you are aware,
                    when treaties are transmitted to the Senate to receive its advice and consent to
                    their ratification they are usually accompanied by a report from the Secretary
                    of State to the President. A draft of such a report has been prepared and a copy
                    enclosed.</p>
                <p>In view of your close association with Mr. Byrnes and the Delegation in the
                    formulation of these Treaties I am sending you this copy in advance and would
                    welcome any suggestions you might care to make in connection therewith.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
